.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt CLAUDE-STEPBOARD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm claude-stepboard
.Nd the Claude Code CLI in a browser tab, with a panel of prompt buttons beside it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm use
.Nm
.Cm dev
.Nm
.Cm ls
.Nm
.Cm stop
.Op Ar N | Cm all
.Op Fl -keep
.Nm
.Cm man
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl -help | Cm help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
starts a StepBoard session: the real
.Xr claude 1
running in a
.Xr tmux 1
session, a terminal bridge
.Pq Xr ttyd 1
on a private unix socket, a small FastAPI server, and a Safari tab that draws
the terminal on the left and the panel on the right.
.Pp
Every run adds an independent session
.Ar N ,
starting at 1.
When a session is already running,
.Nm
asks
.Sq create session N? [Y/n] ;
Enter means yes.
.Pp
The claude process lives in tmux, not in the browser.
Reloading or closing the tab, or pressing Ctrl-C in the launcher window,
leaves it running, and the next launch re-attaches to it.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm use
The default.
Serves the built panel
.Pq Pa ui/dist
from the API server on port 8000+N: no Node, no reloader, about 80 MB per
session.
Rebuilds
.Pa ui/dist
first if anything under
.Pa ui/
is newer than it.
.It Cm dev
For working on StepBoard itself.
Vite serves the panel on port 5172+N with hot reload, and the API server
restarts when
.Pa serve.py
changes.
About 480 MB per session.
.It Cm ls
Lists running sessions: the board
.Pq mode and URL
and whether claude is alive in tmux
.Li sb Ns Ar N .
.It Cm stop Oo Ar N | Cm all Oc Op Fl -keep
Closes session
.Ar N :
stops its servers, closes its Safari tab and ends tmux session
.Li sb Ns Ar N .
With
.Fl -keep ,
claude stays running in tmux so the next launch re-attaches.
.Cm all
closes every session.
Without
.Ar N ,
it acts only when exactly one board is running.
.Pp
It only ever touches what the launcher recorded in its run file and the exact
tmux session name \(em never a name pattern, never the tmux server, never a
claude outside
.Li sb Ns Ar N .
The chat is saved on disk either way;
.Li /resume
in claude brings it back.
.It Cm man
Shows this page.
.It Fl h , Fl -help , Cm help
Prints a one-screen summary.
.El
.Sh SESSIONS
.Bl -column "session" "sbN" "$TMPDIR/stepboard-N.sock" "8000+N" "5172+N"
.It Em session Ta Em tmux Ta Em terminal socket Ta Em panel Ta Em dev panel
.It 1 Ta sb1 Ta $TMPDIR/stepboard-1.sock Ta 8001 Ta 5173
.It 2 Ta sb2 Ta $TMPDIR/stepboard-2.sock Ta 8002 Ta 5174
.It N Ta sbN Ta $TMPDIR/stepboard-N.sock Ta 8000+N Ta 5172+N
.El
.Sh KEYS
In the panel
.Pq also listed in its SHORTCUTS card :
.Bl -tag -width "Cm Ctrl-Shift-Q"
.It Cm Cmd-J
Jump to the terminal.
.It Cm Cmd-K
Jump to the composer.
.It Cm Cmd-Shift-L
Grab the terminal selection into the composer
.Pq Cm Ctrl-Shift-L No too .
.It Cm Option-1..9
Arm or disarm prompt 1..9.
.It Cm Return
Send, from anywhere outside the terminal.
.It Cm Ctrl-Shift-Q
Close this StepBoard.
It asks first: Return closes everything, Option-Return keeps claude
running, Escape cancels.
.It Cm Shift-Return
New line, in the composer and in the terminal.
.It Cm Up , Cm Down
Walk the history once the caret is at the edge of the composer.
.It Cm Cmd-A
Select all of the draft.
.It Cm drag
Select text in the terminal; it is copied to the clipboard.
.It Cm Escape
In the prompt editor: back out of the delete confirm, then the form, then
edit mode.
.El
.Pp
Lines starting with
.Ql /command
or
.Ql \&!shell
are sent exactly as typed.
Anything else gets the armed prompts and the Length/Format/Edits clauses
appended; the line under the composer shows what.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev TMPDIR
Where the run files and sockets live
.Pq default Pa /tmp .
.It Ev SB_SESSION , Ev SB_TTYD_SOCK , Ev SB_PROMPTS
Set by the launcher for
.Pa serve.py ;
set them yourself only to run the server by hand, e.g. for the tests.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $TMPDIR/stepboard-N.run
The launcher's PID and its children's PIDs.
.Cm stop
reads it; the launcher removes it on exit.
.It Pa $TMPDIR/stepboard-N.sock
The ttyd socket.
Only local processes can reach it; the page talks to it through
.Pa /api/ws .
.It Pa prompts.json
The prompt buttons, next to
.Pa serve.py ,
shared by every session.
.Ev SB_PROMPTS
moves it.
.It Pa ~/.claude/projects/
Where claude keeps the chat, which is what
.Li /resume
reads.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Answering no to
.Sq create session N?
also exits 0.
A wrong command or an ambiguous bare
.Cm stop
exits 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start the default board and open it in Safari:
.Dl claude-stepboard
.Pp
Hack on the panel with hot reload:
.Dl claude-stepboard dev
.Pp
Restart a board to pick up new code, keeping claude alive:
.Dl claude-stepboard stop 2 --keep && claude-stepboard
.Pp
Close everything:
.Dl claude-stepboard stop all
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr claude 1 ,
.Xr tmux 1 ,
.Xr ttyd 1
.Pp
.Pa README.md
and
.Pa SUMMARY.md
in the repository.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
A web terminal is a full shell.
ttyd has no TCP port.
The API refuses any Host other than localhost or 127.0.0.1 and any
cross-site Origin, which blocks DNS rebinding and cross-site WebSocket
hijacking.
